# Resolve only after scripts/run_piper_training_readiness.py reports ready=true
# inside CPython 3.11 / x86_64 WSL2. This is an input specification, not an
# installable hash lock. The final lock must be generated and probed in WSL2.
# PyTorch is deliberately resolved by the separate piper-f1-torch.in so this
# PyPI resolution cannot silently select a CPU or different CUDA wheel.

# Exact constraints copied from piper1-gpl v1.6.0 at commit
# f04d52c5528ac7cf2d73757f57990ff490f75005. Piper itself is installed from
# that source revision only after the dependency lock and checkpoint probe pass.
